oh look  another glorious morning  makes me sick  hocus pocus  this walt disney pictures film was a  huge flop at the box office in 1993 but  has since become a beloved cult classic  rewashed by millions every halloween  season  but how and why did hocus pocus go from  such a disaster to a must-watch seasonal  movie  welcome back everyone to stream in the  galaxy my name is rocket riley and today  we're going to be talking about the 1993  disney film hocus pocus and why people  seem to be so obsessed with it but  before we get started if you're new to  the channel please hit the subscribe  button and click the bell icon to be  notified when we upload a new video  at its initial release in july of 1993  hocus pocus was a flop at the box office  earning only 39 million dollars that's  right the halloween themed movie was  released in july only a month after the  smash hit jurassic park  because of a weak marketing campaign  poor critic reviews and the marginal  desire for a halloween movie during the  summer hocus pocus did not do so well  now however the film has made waves in  popularity as it's basically been played  on repeat for two decades on freeform  and abc family during the month of  october  it's these continual reruns which  initially set off the hocus pocus craze  kids and even adults would watch the  movie once or maybe four times every  year during the abc family 31 nights of  halloween  now 20 years later these kids have grown  up and built a great sense of nostalgia  for the film because they've come to  either have a strong association between  hocus pocus and their fond halloween  memories or because it's one of their  yearly must-do rituals  but where does this sense of nostalgia  come from the short answer  the nostalgia really comes from people  remembering what it felt like to be a  child watching the sanderson sisters  perform i put a spell on you during the  halloween season it makes us feel  connected not only to a time long past  but to everyone else who shares those  memories with us  it likely all started due to the fact  that many parents only allowed their  kids to watch three different halloween  themed movies hocus pocus halloween town  and the nightmare before christmas  all of these movies have strong cult  followings stemming from the same basic  principles that building an association  between a movie and a certain time of  year will improve the movie's yearly  rewatch ability and that creating a  strong sense of nostalgia will generate  better long-term profits  now there are some more specific  elements of the film which help  contribute to our obsession with hocus  pocus  first of all while it's not too scary  for a child hearing the phrase it's all  just a bunch of hocus pocus does sort of  send shivers down your spine when you  know it's not just hocus pocus also who  doesn't love our favorite feline friend  thackery binks you know banks i'll  always take care of you  my children will take care of you too  and their children after that  and theirs after that  the way the movie related to the kids  watching was also done in a way that  only disney movies did at the time  calling school a prison for children  just reassured millions of kids that  they were right and that adults were the  ones who were wrong  also don't forget that max had basically  the coolest room in the world at the top  of their colonial salem massachusetts  home  the movie also introduced tons of new  words to our vocabularies like virgin  yabbos and many more  wedge  trollop  you  bucktooth  [Applause]  mostly the general cheesiness and crazy  hijinks that we all secretly wish to be  a part of just set us in the halloween  mood whether it be the iconic costumes  and looks of the sanderson sisters or  the wonderfully terrible cgi used  throughout the film every bit of hocus  pocus drives the sense of nostalgia  deeper making those warm fuzzy feelings  bubble back up to the surface  hocus pocus truly is worthy of the  obsession so many people hold for it  well that's going to be everything from  us today on hocus pocus if you enjoyed  the video please hit the like button and  don't forget to subscribe for more great  content what's your favorite hocus-pocus  memory drop in the comment section below  from everyone here at stream in the  galaxy we hope you have a great day and  thanks for watching  you

